WEBVTT

NOTE Descriptive captions for silent native beta footage; no spoken audio.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
Let's ask a question we can check against a file.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.000
A turn includes the work between our message and the answer.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Navlog reads the aircraft profile and checks memory.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:25.000
Open the readDoc activity to see its arguments and result.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:34.000
The profile specifies a Cessna 172N, 50 US gal usable fuel, and 2400 RPM.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Now ask a follow-up: what does the same file say about reserve fuel?

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:47.000
This is a second turn, with a new file read and memory lookup.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:54.000
The answer arrives. Compare it with the returned profile.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Reserve: 45 min at planned cruise burn. The profile has no alternate-fuel entry.
